course: dictionary
lesson: 2109
title: Contributor: one word, several meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A contributor is someone or something that gives to a group, a project or a result. Most often it means a person who helps by giving money, ideas or work. «Rust was backed by Mozilla, and it is now open source with many contributors.» The contributors are the people who gave their work to build Rust.
explain: The word's shape gives a clue. Contribute means to give, and the ending -or often means the person or thing that does the action. So a contributor is a giver. Ask yourself: who is giving, and what are they giving? Then check your answer against the sentence.
explain: Read the words around it, because the meaning can change. «Smoking is a major contributor to heart disease» does not mean a person. Here a contributor is a thing that helps cause something bad. The phrase «a major contributor to» tells you that.
explain: Watch out for words on school reports. «Josh is an enthusiastic contributor» can sound like praise, but a teacher may mean Josh shouts out answers without waiting. The context and what the writer is really saying tell you the meaning.
fact: A contributor is someone who gives money, help or ideas to something together with others.
fact: A contributor can also be a person who writes articles or parts for a book, magazine, website or project.
fact: A contributor can be a thing that helps cause something, such as smoking being a major contributor to heart disease.
fact: Useful phrases include «a major contributor to», «a regular contributor» and «list of contributors».
fact: «Enthusiastic contributor» can mean a pupil who shouts out answers without waiting, so always check the context.
exercise: «Rust was backed by Mozilla, and it is now open source with many contributors.» Who are the contributors in this sentence? | The computers that Rust runs on | Only the people who ate lunch at Mozilla | *People who gave their work and ideas to Rust | The year 2015
exercise: «Smoking is a major contributor to heart disease.» In this sentence, what is a contributor? | A doctor who gives money to charity | *A thing that helps cause heart disease | A person who writes a school report
exercise: The word contribute means to give. What does a contributor do? | Waits quietly for a turn | Writes school reports | *Gives money, help or ideas
test: On a school report, «Josh is an enthusiastic contributor» might mean | Josh is very kind to animals | Josh writes the best stories | Josh is the class leader | *Josh shouts out answers without waiting
test: «She is a regular contributor to the magazine.» This means she | Draws the front cover only | *Writes parts for the magazine often | Sells the magazine in shops | Reads the magazine once a year
exam: In «The charity thanked its contributors», contributors means | The shop workers who sold the cakes | Lost property left at the event | *People who gave money, help or ideas | The charity's buildings and offices
